  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:H8YAGOB5Xck",
    "purpose": "Compare six well-known down jackets, explaining what makes each one distinct (fabric, denier, insulation, waterproofing, ageing, history), and name a favourite.",
    "video_type": "comparison",
    "thesis": "Each of six down jackets has a specific property that sets it apart. The video works through fabric basics (denier, nylon versus cotton, Gore-Tex versus wax) and each jacket's trade-offs. It names the Crescent Down Works x Imogene + Willie hoodie as the creator's favourite and The North Face Nuptse as second.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Covers The North Face Nuptse, Patagonia Cotton Down Jacket, Fjällräven Greenland No. 1 down jacket, the historic Karakoram jacket, Arc'teryx Beta Down Insulated Jacket and the Crescent Down Works x Imogene + Willie hooded jacket.",
      "Explains denier as a measure of fibre weight. Lower denier is softer and silkier; higher denier is thicker and stronger (40D vs 1000D nylon).",
      "Nylon is described as about twice as strong as cotton for its weight. Cotton breathes better but absorbs water and dries slowly.",
      "Discusses a cotton jacket with a reapplicable DWR finish as an option for everyday, non-extreme use.",
      "A waxable jacket lets the wearer choose between breathability (unwaxed) and weather resistance (waxed), and wax ages differently from Gore-Tex, which can delaminate.",
      "Retells the 1953 K2 expedition belay, in which Pete Schoening (named in the captions as Shonen) arrested the fall of six climbers. The Karakoram jacket is tied to that expedition.",
      "The Arc'teryx Beta Down mixes 800 fill down with synthetic insulation in wet-prone areas and uses a Gore-Tex shell. Its main long-term issue is adhesive delamination.",
      "The Crescent Down Works hoodie uses sewn-through seams (cold spots), premium Seattle-made down and a white 'streak free' nylon. Its $700 price and how easily it will get dirty are discussed."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Introduction to down jackets",
        "summary": "Teaser of the jackets in the lineup, a plug for the new second channel, and the setup of six down jackets each with a special property. Ranking hints are given.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "The North Face Nuptse and denier",
        "summary": "The Nuptse as a stylish, warm 700 fill nylon jacket that is part of a layering system. Explains what denier means, comparing 1000D and 40D nylon.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Fabric strength comparison",
        "summary": "Nylon versus cotton strength, noting nylon is roughly twice as strong for its weight.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Sponsor message",
        "summary": "Sponsor read for the Carrot discount app and browser extension.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Patagonia cotton jacket",
        "summary": "The $395 Patagonia cotton down jacket: slim fit, breathability of cotton versus nylon or polyester, cotton's downsides when wet, and DWR finishes. Compared with the North Face.",
        "first_segment": 4,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "Fjällräven jacket review",
        "summary": "Why the waxable Fjällräven down jacket is often recommended. Covers durability, thorn resistance, ageing, waxing versus not waxing (compared with L.L.Bean boots), and wax versus Gore-Tex for water resistance.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 7
      },
      {
        "title": "Historic Karakoram jacket",
        "summary": "The Karakoram down jacket and the story of the 1953 K2 expedition. Retells the famous belay that saved six climbers, with a comedic dramatization.",
        "first_segment": 7,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Arc'teryx tech jacket",
        "summary": "The Arc'teryx Beta Down Insulated Jacket's technical construction: 800 fill down plus synthetic insulation in wet zones and a Gore-Tex shell. Also covers delamination and how it ages compared with nylon, waxed or cotton jackets.",
        "first_segment": 8,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Crescent Down Works review",
        "summary": "The Crescent Down Works x Imogene + Willie hooded jacket: history of the Seattle company, sewn-through construction, premium materials and looks. Covers the price dilemma and the white streak-free nylon, then teases next week's wool jacket video.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 12
      }
    ],
